# lint_eval_roster: one that has no row here fails the gate, and so does a
# row nothing matches.
#
#   eval|<file>|<what it evaluates>|<the line from `eval` on, 72 characters>
#   <kin>|<file>|<how many>
#
# <what it evaluates>:
#   const    a literal the file spells, kept from a parser that cannot read it
#   name     a variable or function name hi chose; values go by reference
#   own      hi's own words as code: an exit hook's command, a prompt escape
#   shell    the shell's own listing run back: complete -p, alias -p, trap -p
#   tool     a prompt program's init, which is how it installs itself
#   segment  an extension's $_HI_SEGMENT, a command by contract (GLOSSARY: HI.59)
# The last three read text from outside the tree.
#
# <kin>: `source` is a source or . of a path held in a variable, `sh -c` a
# shell handed a script in a word, `rm -r` a recursive delete.

